# Keep build detritus out of the context.
#
# `patch` leaves a .orig beside every file it touches when it has to save one,
# and the Dockerfile applies patches/ with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0`. If a .orig from
# an earlier run is in the context, the next run refuses to create it again and
# the build fails with "The next patch would create the file ...". That already
# happened once. The file is worthless either way, so never ship it.
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/target/
builds/
node_modules/
javascript/
*.s9pk
